From 05c79442673927d15735ccc0d411f4bf397fc52c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thierry Laurion <insurgo@riseup.net>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:10:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] soc/intel/alderlake: issue APM_CNT_GPIO_LOCK before the
 payload

Refs: "TPM GPIO fail" https://mkukri.xyz/2024-06-01/tpm-gpio-fail.html ; coreboot ticket #576 ; https://github.com/tlaurion/tpm-gpio-fail

soc_finalize() runs at BS_PAYLOAD_BOOT and BS_OS_RESUME, after FSP-S has
run its notify phases and unlocked every GPIO pad, and before the
payload is entered. That is exactly where the PLTRST# pad has to be
locked, and it is the earliest point at which it can be: locking it
earlier, in the romstage, is a no-op, because FSP-S unlocks every pad
in its notify phases.

Issue the dedicated APM_CNT_GPIO_LOCK SMI from there. The lock runs in
the SMM handler, where the P2SB can be unhidden and the sideband
interface lock message is honored: up to and including Alder Lake PCH
the pad configuration lock registers can only be written through the
sideband interface (Intel document 834810), and that access is armed
for the SMI handler context, not for bare pre-payload stages. Calling
the lock directly from the ramstage instead dies in p2sb_dev_unhide(),
because the P2SB cannot be unhidden at that point (observed on the
NV4x).

The pad is therefore locked before anything after the firmware can
run, without depending on INTEL_CHIPSET_LOCKDOWN, on the payload, or on
APM_CNT_FINALIZE being issued at all. PR0/FLOCKDN keep their existing
timing: the payload-issued APM_CNT_FINALIZE performs the SPI and LPC
lockdown and ends with the sideband lock; when it re-locks the pad it
is a write of a bit that is already set, verified by the readback.

Signed-off-by: Thierry Laurion <insurgo@riseup.net>
Heads-Note: heads-specific, no upstream equivalent; carried against coreboot-dasharo_nv4x 281a7fec1a1e;
	applies unmodified to the pinned fork.

---
 src/soc/intel/alderlake/finalize.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/soc/intel/alderlake/finalize.c b/src/soc/intel/alderlake/finalize.c
index 615729d..cdd8f9f 100644
--- a/src/soc/intel/alderlake/finalize.c
+++ b/src/soc/intel/alderlake/finalize.c
@@ -85,6 +85,16 @@ static void soc_finalize(void *unused)
 	printk(BIOS_DEBUG, "Finalizing chipset.\n");
 
 	pch_finalize();
+	/*
+	 * Lock the PLTRST# pad configuration from its own SMI, before the
+	 * payload is entered. The SMI handler locks only the pads from
+	 * soc_gpio_lock_config(); it does not run the SPI and LPC lockdown
+	 * and does not lock down the sideband interface, so the
+	 * payload-issued APM_CNT_FINALIZE keeps its own timing for
+	 * PR0/FLOCKDN.
+	 */
+	if (CONFIG(SOC_INTEL_COMMON_BLOCK_GPIO_LOCK_PLTRST_PAD))
+		apm_control(APM_CNT_GPIO_LOCK);
 	if (CONFIG(INTEL_CHIPSET_LOCKDOWN) || acpi_is_wakeup_s3())
 		apm_control(APM_CNT_FINALIZE);
 
